# KEUR-DOC-005 — README carries the two essential chapters (CMMI-1 floor).
# @implements ADR-061, docs/design/doc-chapter-contract.md, ADR-011 (maturity gate)
#
# absence engine: fires per chapter whose canonical heading AND none of its
# agreed aliases appear in README.md. These are the two the chapter contract
# marks "Required from CMMI-1". The other four README chapters are DOC-005b.
#
# CLOSED ALIAS SET, not free synonyms (contract rationale): keur accepts the
# canonical heading or an agreed alias listed in doc-chapter-contract.md, and
# rejects an unlisted word. The alternation below IS that closed set. A new
# alias is added to the contract (one place), not here per repo. The regex
# anchors on an H2+ heading and matches case-insensitively.
id: KEUR-DOC-005
ilities: [analysability]
maturity: 1
title: README is missing an essential chapter (Context / Local setup)
category: quality
severity: warning
engine: absence
action: warn
skip_emoji: true
target:
  filenames: README.md
patterns:
  - regex: (?im)^#{2,}\s+(Context|Overview|About|Introduction)\b
    message: "README has no Context chapter. The contract (doc-chapter-contract.md) requires it from CMMI-1 — accepted headings: Context (canonical), Overview, About, Introduction."
  - regex: (?im)^#{2,}\s+(Local setup|Getting started|Install|Installation|Usage|Quick ?start)\b
    message: "README has no Local setup chapter. Required from CMMI-1 — accepted headings: Local setup (canonical), Getting started, Install, Installation, Usage, Quick start."
confidence: 0.6
fix: "Add the chapter using the canonical heading or an agreed alias (see docs/design/doc-chapter-contract.md). The remaining four README chapters — Prerequisites, Validate, Release, More info — are required from CMMI-2 (DOC-005b)."
